{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Google Docstring Reminder",
  "description": "Remind to add Google-style docstrings when saving Python files with public functions",
  "version": "2",
  "when": {
    "type": "onFileSave",
    "patterns": ["backend/**/*.py", "api/**/*.py"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "sendMessage",
    "message": "Check that any new or modified public functions/classes have Google-style docstrings. Format: one-line summary, blank line, Args section with types, Returns section, Raises section if applicable. Example:\n\n```python\ndef function_name(arg1: str, arg2: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Short one-line summary of function.\n\n    Longer description if needed.\n\n    Args:\n        arg1: Description of arg1.\n        arg2: Description of arg2.\n\n    Returns:\n        Description of return value.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: When arg1 is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nOnly add docstrings to public functions (not underscore-prefixed). Keep them concise."
  }
}
